    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file 'extract_json.py' that calls a hosted LLM to extract structured JSON from text, I will use the Amazon Bedrock service, which is a concrete external provider. The code will import the necessary Bedrock client and use a specific model identifier to make the integration identifiable. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789850167401,
          "start": 1789850164797
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bb621e3d001L0n57KfYOtRApz",
